camchrome: WebRTC over the SOCKS5 relay finds the exit IP by itself

100 hides the real IP by fabricating the server-reflexive candidate at --webrtc-ip, which the user
must look up and pass by hand, and which is wrong as soon as a rotating proxy changes exit. With
973/990 every P2P UDP socket already leaves through the proxy's relay, so a real STUN binding
request reports the proxy's exit IP on its own.

  * The browser appends --webrtc-socks5-relay to each renderer when it runs with --socks5-udp and a
    SOCKS5 --proxy-server (the proxy URL itself stays out of the renderer).
  * In the renderer, that switch without an IP-literal --webrtc-ip (absent, or --webrtc-ip=auto)
    turns on relay mode: candidate gathering is forced on as for --webrtc-ip, STUN runs for real
    (through the relay), host candidates are suppressed (they would name the local socket) and the
    srflx candidate's related address is emptied (it would carry the default local address).
  * An explicit --webrtc-ip=<ip> keeps 100's behaviour: no STUN packet, fabricated srflx.

Use --webrtc-ip=auto only together with --socks5-udp and a SOCKS5 proxy: without the relay, STUN
would leave from the real interface.
